# geek-platform

The Waveshare GEEK family: two USB-stick boards, the RP2040-GEEK and the
RP2350-GEEK, and the panel provider they share. Both carry a 1.14 inch 240 by
135 IPS panel on an ST7789, a TF card socket, a USB-A plug on the native port,
and three small headers -- a four-pin I2C port and two three-pin ports, the one
labelled SWD and the one labelled UART, laid out as the Raspberry Pi Debug
Probe's ports are -- and both schematics wire them to the same GPIOs, so the
panel's wiring is written once.

rp2040_geek derives from pico and rp2350_geek from pico2-arm; neither can
derive from the other, because the chip is what the base supplies. Each binds
platform.geek.display, the panel, and platform.geek.sdcard, the TF socket on
SPI0 as mm.sdcard.socket. The device drivers are the portable mm.lcd.st7789
and mm.sdcard, and the providers are the only place that knows which pin is
which.
